        {
          "supplier": "thm-tonelli-theorem-for-sigma-finite-product-spaces",
          "carrier": "items/thm-tonelli-theorem-for-sigma-finite-product-spaces.md",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "exact_statement": "Let $(X,\\mathcal A,\\mu)$ and $(Y,\\mathcal B,\\nu)$ be sigma-finite measure\nspaces, and let $f : X \\times Y \\to [0,\\infty]$ be product-measurable. Then\n$x \\mapsto \\int_Y f_x\\,d\\nu$ and $y \\mapsto \\int_X f^y\\,d\\mu$ are measurable,\nand\n\n$$\\int_{X \\times Y} f\\,d(\\mu \\times \\nu) = \\int_X \\left(\\int_Y f_x\\,d\\nu\\right)d\\mu = \\int_Y \\left(\\int_X f^y\\,d\\mu\\right)d\\nu.$$",
