      "citations": [
        {
          "fact": "F1",
          "source": "thm-nrqmx-finite-channel-wigner-smith",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $I\\subset\\mathbb R$ be an open energy interval with fixed finite channel number $r\\ge1$, let $S:I\\to U(r)$ be $C^1$ in the finite-channel convention of [[def-nrqmx-scattering-channel-data]], and let $\\hbar>0$. Define\n\n$$Q(E):=-i\\hbar\\,S(E)^*S'(E),\\qquad E\\in I.$$\n\nThen $Q(E)$ is Hermitian and\n\n$$\\operatorname{tr}Q(E) =-i\\hbar\\,\\frac{(\\det S)'(E)}{\\det S(E)} =-i\\hbar\\,\\frac{d}{dE}\\log\\det S(E),$$\n\nwhere the last expression means the logarithmic derivative $(\\det S)'/\\det S$, independent of a choice of logarithm branch. If the incoming and outgoing bases are changed by energy-independent unitary matrices $U_{\\mathrm{in}}$ and $U_{\\mathrm{out}}$, so that $S^\\sharp=U_{\\mathrm{out}}^*SU_{\\mathrm{in}}$, then\n\n$$Q^\\sharp=U_{\\mathrm{in}}^* Q U_{\\mathrm{in}}.$$\n\nIf $E$ is measured in joules and $\\hbar$ in joule-seconds, $Q$ has units of seconds. This is an algebraic scattering-matrix result; it does not by itself establish an operational arrival-time or dwell-time interpretation.",
          "uses": [
            "2.1"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "derivations": [
        {
          "id": "step-1-1",
          "claim": "Since $\\delta(E)$ is real, $S(E)^*S(E)=e^{-2i\\delta(E)}e^{2i\\delta(E)}=1$; thus this is a one-channel unitary matrix on all of $I$. Differentiation gives $S'(E)=2i\\delta'(E)e^{2i\\delta(E)}$.",
          "step": "1.1",
          "inputs": [
            "given",
            "algebra"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "step-2-1",
          "claim": "Substitution into [F1] gives $Q(E)=-i\\hbar e^{-2i\\delta(E)}2i\\delta'(E)e^{2i\\delta(E)}=2\\hbar\\delta'(E)$, which is real. Since $\\delta$ is dimensionless and $d\\delta/dE$ has units $\\mathrm J^{-1}$, $Q$ has units $\\mathrm s$. No pointwise value of $Q$ is interpreted as a measured time.",
          "step": "2.1",
          "inputs": [
            "given",
            "F1",
            "step 1.1",
            "algebra"
          ]
        }
      ],
